## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to combine streaming validation, dual sinks (S3 and DynamoDB), and a simple streaming analytics path. It adds a new analytics angle (rolling average) with per-record validation and a dead-letter queue, plus distributed tracing and local testing capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams and Firehose for real-time data ingestion and delivery
- Lambda-based validation with SQS DLQ routing for error handling
- S3 Parquet format with hourly time-based partitioning
- Kinesis Data Analytics for windowed stream aggregations
- DynamoDB for persisting computed metrics
- AWS X-Ray for end-to-end distributed tracing
- LocalStack for local integration testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lambda validator with DLQ routing (pseudo-code)
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const dlqPromises = [];
  const validRecords = [];

  for (const record of event.records) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(record.data, 'base64').toString());

    const validation = validateTelemetry(payload);
    if (!validation.valid) {
      dlqPromises.push(sendToDLQ({ payload, error: validation.error }));
    } else {
      validRecords.push(record);
    }
  }

  await Promise.all(dlqPromises);
  return { records: validRecords.map(r => ({ recordId: r.recordId, result: 'Ok' })) };
};

function validateTelemetry(payload) {
  const required = ['deviceId', 'temperature', 'timestamp'];
  const missing = required.filter(f => !payload[f]);
  if (missing.length > 0) return { valid: false, error: `Missing fields: ${missing.join(', ')}` };
  if (typeof payload.temperature !== 'number' || payload.temperature < -50 || payload.temperature > 150) {
    return { valid: false, error: 'Temperature out of range' };
  }
  return { valid: true };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to architect a multi-tenant data pipeline with configurable reliability guarantees, encompassing tenant isolation, fault tolerance, performance optimization, and comprehensive observability—all critical for enterprise-grade streaming solutions.

## Key Concepts

- **Tenant Partitioning**: Dedicated Kinesis streams per tenant with isolated processing contexts
- **Processing Guarantees**: Exactly-once semantics via DynamoDB deduplication vs. at-least-once with retry mechanisms
- **Backpressure Management**: Dynamic shard autoscaling and Lambda concurrency controls based on SLA requirements
- **Observability**: OpenTelemetry integration for end-to-end monitoring and performance metrics
- **Audit & Compliance**: S3 metadata tracking and Glue catalog for data lineage and governance
- **Cost Optimization**: Per-tenant resource allocation and usage-based cost attribution

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: tenant-aware deduplication and persistence
async function persistTelemetryEvent(ctx, event) {
  const deduplicationKey = `${ctx.tenantId}:${event.eventId}`;

  // Check for existing event to ensure exactly-once semantics
  const existingEvent = await checkDeduplication(deduplicationKey);
  if (!existingEvent) {
    await writeToProcessedSink(ctx.tenantId, event);
    await recordDeduplication(deduplicationKey);
  }

  // Update tenant-specific metrics for cost accounting
  await updateTenantMetrics(ctx.tenantId, event.size);
}
```

